content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23500 (55 kW, 1480 rpm)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 85 C (handheld IR gun). The HF-300 limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C and trip 90 C. The reading is 5 C above the alarm limit and 5 C below the trip limit, so it is in the alarm band. It is measured on the housing surface, as the manual specifies.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 2.5 mm/s. Against HF-300 Figure 3 (mm/s RMS on bearing housings) this is Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s, 'New machines'). It is below the 2.8 mm/s A/B boundary and well below the 4.5 mm/s (restricted) and 7.1 mm/s (stop the pump) boundaries. Vibration does not require action.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage at the shaft seal and no noise are reported. The 'Leakage at shaft seal' symptom does not apply, so seal replacement is not indicated.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall: the temperature is in alarm but below trip, and vibration is in Zone A. No document criterion calls for an immediate stop. The trip limit is only 5 C away, so trend the temperature closely and stop at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the drive-end bearing. This is the first listed cause of high bearing temperature, and it fits best with low vibration (Zone A) and no noise.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear. This is a listed cause of high bearing temperature, but it is less likely given low vibration and no noise.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is a listed cause of high bearing temperature (and of high vibration), but it is less likely because vibration is in Zone A.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the reading. Re-measure DE and NDE bearing housing surface temperatures, and measure vibration on both bearing housings. Classify the highest vibration reading against Figure 3 (mm/s RMS). If DE temperature reaches the 90 C trip limit, stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the DE bearing (troubleshooting action for high bearing temperature). Correct any over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the temperature does not return toward the normal range (≤70 C), isolate the pump and inspect the bearings for wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair per section 5.3: DE HF3-512 (6312-C3) and NDE HF3-510 (6310-C3).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, tighten fasteners to Table 5: bearing housing bolts M12 at 85 Nm, impeller nut M24 at 160 Nm (if disturbed), and casing bolts M16 at 210 Nm (if the casing joint is opened). Threads should be lightly oiled.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the mechanical seal is disturbed, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B (not HF3-450) and torque the seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, per SB-2026-014. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120 if the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. This is required after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and is also a high-temperature troubleshooting check. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, confirm DE bearing housing temperature is ≤70 C (normal) and vibration remains in Zone A/B. Record the readings for weekly condition monitoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (conditional – only if bearing wear is found; replace as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (conditional – replaced as a pair with the DE bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (conditional – replace whenever the casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, supersedes HF3-450 for serial ≥ HF3-22000 (conditional – only if the seal is disturbed)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before any intrusive work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so use lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge. Never run the pump dry, including during test runs after reassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bearing housing is hot (85 C measured). Stop the pump if the temperature reaches the 90 C trip limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical fitter for the grease check, bearing inspection and replacement, and a laser alignment tool for alignment. Lifting equipment and a second person are needed if the 68 kg back pull-out assembly is removed. Durations are not given in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal: the manual parts list and section 5.2 specify component seal HF3-450 and gland nut torque 25 Nm (Table 5). Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (14 March 2026) applies to HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. It supersedes this with cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm gland torque. P-109 is serial HF3-23500, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies: use HF3-450B and 30 Nm. All other Table 5 torques remain as per the manual.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Grease type, quantity per bearing and regreasing interval are not given in the evidence, so the 'check grease quantity' step has no reference value.",
    "Is the 2.5 mm/s reading velocity RMS, and was it taken on both bearing housings? Figure 3 is in mm/s RMS, and the highest housing reading must be used.",
    "NDE bearing housing temperature is not reported.",
    "IR gun emissivity/accuracy versus a contact measurement is not addressed; the 85 C reading should be confirmed.",
    "The evidence does not state whether bearing replacement requires removing the seal or opening the casing, so the need for HF3-450B and HF3-120 is uncertain.",
    "No labour hours or crew size are given in the documents.",
    "No bearing fit/clearance, grease fill or lubrication procedure is given for section 5.3 beyond 'replace both bearings as a pair'.",
    "The manual Revision D issue date is not given, so it cannot be confirmed that SB-2026-014 is newer than the manual (the serial-range applicability is clear, however)."
  ]
}
